{"explanation":"For a quadratic equation, the discriminant \(D=b^2-4ac\) determines how the parabola meets the x-axis: positive means two intersections (two distinct real roots), zero means it touches once (one repeated real root), and negative means no real intersections (no real roots). The visualization uses \(x^2+c=0\), whose discriminant is \(-4c\), so moving the slider across \(c=0\) shows all three cases.","manimCode":"const ax = new Axes({
  xRange: [-2, 2, 1],
  yRange: [-1.5, 3, 1],
  xLength: 8,
  yLength: 4.5,
  tips: true
});
scene.add(ax, ax.getAxisLabels());

let c = -1;
let curve = ax.plot(x => x * x + c, { color: BLUE, numSamples: 240 });
scene.add(curve);

const title = new Text({ text: 'x² + c = 0', color: WHITE, fontSize: 34 });
title.moveTo([-3.8, 3.05, 0]);
